 * every surface (chat card buttons, in-app feed buttons, the peek link).
 *
 * WHY a declaration rather than per-surface construction: the chat card used to
 * build its buttons straight from `runId` while the in-app feed re-derived the
 * run from notification metadata — which stores `resource_type: "event"`, so the
 * lookup failed and the web silently rendered a link-only card. A single
 * declaration means a surface can only fail to render actions, never fail to
 * know about them.
